chx:X_BlockIsHeaderPlusTransactions a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BlockIsHeaderPlusTransactions ; rdfs:label "the 285 bytes of the genesis block"@en ; skos:definition "A block is the 80-byte header, then a counter of the transactions, then the transactions themselves: the genesis block is 80 + 1 + 204 = 285 bytes, and the blocks of the private test chain with 1, 2, 3 and 4 transactions are 250, 472, 694 and 915 bytes, about 222 bytes more for each added transaction."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_BlockIsHeaderPlusTransactions a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('main'); s = {n: R['b4_blocks'][str(n)]['size'] for n in (1, 2, 3, 4)}; (80 + 1 + g['tx_bytes'], R['b1_genesis']['block']['size'], g['tx_bytes'], s, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The block header is 80 bytes')) evaluates to (285, 285, 204, {1: 250, 2: 472, 3: 694, 4: 915}, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('main'); s = {n: R['b4_blocks'][str(n)]['size'] for n in (1, 2, 3, 4)}; (80 + 1 + g['tx_bytes'], R['b1_genesis']['block']['size'], g['tx_bytes'], s, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The block header is 80 bytes'))" ; chx:output "(285, 285, 204, {1: 250, 2: 472, 3: 694, 4: 915}, True)" .
chx:X_BlockIsHeaderPlusTransactions rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BlockIsHeaderPlusTransactions .
chx:X_BlockSizeFieldIsFileStorage a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BlockSizeFieldIsFileStorage ; rdfs:label "the 4-byte size field in front of a block"@en ; skos:definition "The 4-byte block size of the book's table is not part of the block that nodes exchange: it is the field that Bitcoin Core writes in front of each block in its blk file, after the 4 magic bytes, and on the test chain the genesis block was stored with magic fabfb5da and size 285 (293 bytes on disk in all) once the file was read through the XOR key d462ed9f917fe79d that Bitcoin Core has applied to its block files since release 28.0."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_BlockSizeFieldIsFileStorage a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b3_blk_size_field'], R['b3_blk_first_bytes'][:8], R['b3_blk_first_bytes_raw'] != R['b3_blk_first_bytes'], R['b3_xor_key'], R['b3_blk_size_field'] + 8 == R['b1_info0']['size_on_disk'], R['b3_blk_genesis_equals'], L.has('core_relnotes_28.0.md', ('Block files are now XOR' + chr(39) + 'd by default'))) evaluates to (285, 'fabfb5da', True, 'd462ed9f917fe79d', True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b3_blk_size_field'], R['b3_blk_first_bytes'][:8], R['b3_blk_first_bytes_raw'] != R['b3_blk_first_bytes'], R['b3_xor_key'], R['b3_blk_size_field'] + 8 == R['b1_info0']['size_on_disk'], R['b3_blk_genesis_equals'], L.has('core_relnotes_28.0.md', ('Block files are now XOR' + chr(39) + 'd by default')))" ; chx:output "(285, 'fabfb5da', True, 'd462ed9f917fe79d', True, True, True)" .
chx:X_BlockSizeFieldIsFileStorage rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BlockSizeFieldIsFileStorage .
chx:X_TransactionCounter a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TransactionCounter ; rdfs:label "1 to 3 bytes of compactSize"@en ; skos:definition "The transaction counter is a compactSize integer of 1 byte up to 252, 3 bytes for 253 to 65,535 and 5 bytes from 65,536, and a block cannot hold more than 4,000,000 / 240 = 16,666 transactions because the smallest transaction weighs 240 weight units, so the book's 1 to 3 bytes are enough."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_TransactionCounter a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ([len(L.compact_size(n)) for n in (252, 253, 65535, 65536)], 4000000 // (4 * 60), L.has('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'MIN_TRANSACTION_WEIGHT = WITNESS_SCALE_FACTOR * 60'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '1–3 bytes (compactSize)')) evaluates to ([1, 3, 3, 5], 16666, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ([len(L.compact_size(n)) for n in (252, 253, 65535, 65536)], 4000000 // (4 * 60), L.has('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'MIN_TRANSACTION_WEIGHT = WITNESS_SCALE_FACTOR * 60'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '1–3 bytes (compactSize)'))" ; chx:output "([1, 3, 3, 5], 16666, True, True)" .
chx:X_TransactionCounter rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TransactionCounter .
chx:X_GetblockOutputToday a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GetblockOutputToday ; rdfs:label "two new fields since the book"@en ; skos:definition "The getblock listing of Bitcoin Core 31.1 has two fields that the book's listing lacks: target, added by release 29.0, and the coinbase_tx object (version, locktime, sequence, coinbase, witness) that release 31.0 added; the test chain's genesis block shows both, and the book's nextblockhash is absent only because the genesis block was the tip."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_GetblockOutputToday a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); book = {'hash', 'confirmations', 'height', 'version', 'versionHex', 'merkleroot', 'time', 'mediantime', 'nonce', 'bits', 'difficulty', 'chainwork', 'nTx', 'nextblockhash', 'strippedsize', 'size', 'weight', 'tx'}; g = R['b1_genesis']['block']; (sorted(set(g) - book), sorted(book - set(g)), sorted(g['coinbase_tx']), L.has('core_relnotes_29.0.md', 'now return the current target in the `target` field'), L.has('core_relnotes_31.0.txt', 'now returns a coinbase_tx object at verbosity levels 1')) evaluates to (['coinbase_tx', 'target'], ['nextblockhash'], ['coinbase', 'locktime', 'sequence', 'version'], True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); book = {'hash', 'confirmations', 'height', 'version', 'versionHex', 'merkleroot', 'time', 'mediantime', 'nonce', 'bits', 'difficulty', 'chainwork', 'nTx', 'nextblockhash', 'strippedsize', 'size', 'weight', 'tx'}; g = R['b1_genesis']['block']; (sorted(set(g) - book), sorted(book - set(g)), sorted(g['coinbase_tx']), L.has('core_relnotes_29.0.md', 'now return the current target in the `target` field'), L.has('core_relnotes_31.0.txt', 'now returns a coinbase_tx object at verbosity levels 1'))" ; chx:output "(['coinbase_tx', 'target'], ['nextblockhash'], ['coinbase', 'locktime', 'sequence', 'version'], True, True)" .
chx:X_GetblockOutputToday rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GetblockOutputToday .
chx:X_BlockReservedWeight a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BlockReservedWeight ; rdfs:label "8,000 weight units kept back"@en ; skos:definition "Block templates of Bitcoin Core stop short of the consensus limit: -blockreservedweight, default 8000, keeps 8,000 weight units for the header, the counter and the coinbase, so the fullest template is 3,992,000, and block 840,000 with 3,993,281 weight units was made by other software."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_BlockReservedWeight a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', 'plus the largest coinbase transaction the mining software may add to the block', '(default: 8000)'), L.has('core_relnotes_29.0.md', 'will never exceed `3,992,000 WU`'), 4000000 - 8000, L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['weight'] > 4000000 - 8000) evaluates to (True, True, 3992000, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', 'plus the largest coinbase transaction the mining software may add to the block', '(default: 8000)'), L.has('core_relnotes_29.0.md', 'will never exceed `3,992,000 WU`'), 4000000 - 8000, L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['weight'] > 4000000 - 8000)" ; chx:output "(True, True, 3992000, True)" .
chx:X_BlockReservedWeight rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BlockReservedWeight .
chx:X_HeaderIs80Bytes a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HeaderIs80Bytes ; rdfs:label "50,000 headers to a full block"@en ; skos:definition "Every header, of the genesis block, of block 277,315 and of block 120 of the test chain, is exactly 80 bytes, and since MAX_BLOCK_SERIALIZED_SIZE is 4,000,000 a full block can be 4,000,000 / 80 = 50,000 times the header, the book's 'almost 50,000 times'."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_HeaderIs80Bytes a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); hs = [L.raw('mempool_header_0.txt'), L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt'), R['b3_block']['header_hex']]; ([L.header(h)['bytes'] for h in hs], 4000000 // 80, L.const('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'MAX_BLOCK_SERIALIZED_SIZE'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'almost 50,000 times larger')) evaluates to ([80, 80, 80], 50000, '4000000', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); hs = [L.raw('mempool_header_0.txt'), L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt'), R['b3_block']['header_hex']]; ([L.header(h)['bytes'] for h in hs], 4000000 // 80, L.const('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'MAX_BLOCK_SERIALIZED_SIZE'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'almost 50,000 times larger'))" ; chx:output "([80, 80, 80], 50000, '4000000', True)" .
chx:X_HeaderIs80Bytes rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HeaderIs80Bytes .
chx:X_BlockWeightLimit a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BlockWeightLimit ; rdfs:label "block 840,000 at 99.83 percent"@en ; skos:definition "The consensus limit is 4,000,000 weight units, not bytes: block 840,000 held 3,050 transactions with 3,993,281 weight units (99.83 percent of the limit) in only 2,325,617 bytes, 762 bytes per transaction, so a block with witness data can hold less than the 4,000,000 bytes that the book gives as its size."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_BlockWeightLimit a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json'); (L.const('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'MAX_BLOCK_WEIGHT'), b['weight'], b['size'], b['tx_count'], round(100 * b['weight'] / 4000000, 2), round(b['size'] / b['tx_count']), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'can be up to about 4,000,000 bytes')) evaluates to ('4000000', 3993281, 2325617, 3050, 99.83, 762, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json'); (L.const('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'MAX_BLOCK_WEIGHT'), b['weight'], b['size'], b['tx_count'], round(100 * b['weight'] / 4000000, 2), round(b['size'] / b['tx_count']), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'can be up to about 4,000,000 bytes'))" ; chx:output "('4000000', 3993281, 2325617, 3050, 99.83, 762, True)" .
chx:X_BlockWeightLimit rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BlockWeightLimit .
chx:X_VersionBitsField a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:VersionBitsField ; rdfs:label "0x20000000 and the free bits"@en ; skos:definition "The version field is no longer a number but a set of flags: the test chain's blocks carry 0x20000000, the top three bits 001 that BIP 9 requires, while block 840,000 carries 0x2a5fe000, whose bits under the mask 0x1fffe000 (0x0a5fe000) are the 16 bits that the draft BIP 320 reserves for miners to use as extra nonce space."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_VersionBitsField a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['version']; (hex(v), v >> 29, hex(v & 0x1fffe000), R['b3_block']['json']['versionHex'], L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt'))['version'], L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_0.txt'))['version'], L.has('bip-0009.mediawiki', 'The top 3 bits of such blocks must be 001'), L.has('bip-0320.mediawiki', 'Status: Draft', 'Proposed-Replacement: 323')) evaluates to ('0x2a5fe000', 1, '0xa5fe000', '20000000', 2, 1, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['version']; (hex(v), v >> 29, hex(v & 0x1fffe000), R['b3_block']['json']['versionHex'], L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt'))['version'], L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_0.txt'))['version'], L.has('bip-0009.mediawiki', 'The top 3 bits of such blocks must be 001'), L.has('bip-0320.mediawiki', 'Status: Draft', 'Proposed-Replacement: 323'))" ; chx:output "('0x2a5fe000', 1, '0xa5fe000', '20000000', 2, 1, True, True)" .
chx:X_VersionBitsField rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_VersionBitsField .
chx:X_FieldOrderAndEndianness a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:FieldOrderAndEndianness ; rdfs:label "six fields, little-endian"@en ; skos:definition "The six fields in the order of the book's table, with the integers written least significant byte first and the two hashes written in the reverse of the order in which they are displayed, give back exactly the 80 bytes of block 277,315: version 02000000, then the parent hash ending a1632249 in display order, and bits 1903a30c."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_FieldOrderAndEndianness a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); t = L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt'); h = L.header(t); b = h['version'].to_bytes(4, 'little') + bytes.fromhex(h['prev'])[::-1] + bytes.fromhex(h['merkle'])[::-1] + h['time'].to_bytes(4, 'little') + bytes.fromhex(h['bits'])[::-1] + h['nonce'].to_bytes(4, 'little'); (b.hex() == t, len(b), b[:4].hex(), b[4:8].hex(), h['prev'][-8:], h['bits']) evaluates to (True, 80, '02000000', '492263a1', 'a1632249', '1903a30c')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); t = L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt'); h = L.header(t); b = h['version'].to_bytes(4, 'little') + bytes.fromhex(h['prev'])[::-1] + bytes.fromhex(h['merkle'])[::-1] + h['time'].to_bytes(4, 'little') + bytes.fromhex(h['bits'])[::-1] + h['nonce'].to_bytes(4, 'little'); (b.hex() == t, len(b), b[:4].hex(), b[4:8].hex(), h['prev'][-8:], h['bits'])" ; chx:output "(True, 80, '02000000', '492263a1', 'a1632249', '1903a30c')" .
chx:X_FieldOrderAndEndianness rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_FieldOrderAndEndianness .
chx:X_TimestampField a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TimestampField ; rdfs:label "seconds since 1970 in 4 bytes"@en ; skos:definition "The timestamp is a 4-byte count of seconds since 1970-01-01: the genesis block says 2009-01-03 18:15:05 UTC and block 840,000 says 2024-04-20 00:09:27 UTC, a node refuses a block more than 2 x 60 x 60 = 7,200 seconds in the future, and an unsigned 4-byte counter runs out on 2106-02-07 at 06:28:15 UTC."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_TimestampField a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.iso(1231006505), L.iso(2 ** 32 - 1), L.has('core_src_chain.h', 'MAX_FUTURE_BLOCK_TIME = 2 * 60 * 60'), 2 * 60 * 60, L.iso(L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['timestamp']), L.has('wikipedia_unix_time.html', 'Year 2038 problem')) evaluates to ('2009-01-03 18:15:05', '2106-02-07 06:28:15', True, 7200, '2024-04-20 00:09:27', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.iso(1231006505), L.iso(2 ** 32 - 1), L.has('core_src_chain.h', 'MAX_FUTURE_BLOCK_TIME = 2 * 60 * 60'), 2 * 60 * 60, L.iso(L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['timestamp']), L.has('wikipedia_unix_time.html', 'Year 2038 problem'))" ; chx:output "('2009-01-03 18:15:05', '2106-02-07 06:28:15', True, 7200, '2024-04-20 00:09:27', True)" .
chx:X_TimestampField rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TimestampField .
chx:X_MedianTimePast a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MedianTimePast ; rdfs:label "the median of the last 11 timestamps"@en ; skos:definition "A block's timestamp must be later than the median of the previous 11 timestamps: on the test chain this median of blocks 111 to 121 was 1792052132, and block 277,315 of the real chain has a timestamp 1,651 seconds later than its median time past of 1388183387, which BIP 113 uses as the clock for lock times."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_MedianTimePast a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); t = R['b3_timestamps_110_121']; d = L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json'); (L.median_time_past(t), R['b3_mediantime_121'], t[-1] - L.median_time_past(t), d['mediantime'], d['timestamp'], d['timestamp'] - d['mediantime'], L.has('bip-0113.mediawiki', 'median')) evaluates to (1792052132, 1792052132, 0, 1388183387, 1388185038, 1651, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); t = R['b3_timestamps_110_121']; d = L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json'); (L.median_time_past(t), R['b3_mediantime_121'], t[-1] - L.median_time_past(t), d['mediantime'], d['timestamp'], d['timestamp'] - d['mediantime'], L.has('bip-0113.mediawiki', 'median'))" ; chx:output "(1792052132, 1792052132, 0, 1388183387, 1388185038, 1651, True)" .
chx:X_MedianTimePast rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MedianTimePast .
chx:X_TargetCompactEncoding a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TargetCompactEncoding ; rdfs:label "0x1d00ffff and 0x1903a30c"@en ; skos:definition "The 4-byte target field packs a 256-bit number as one byte of exponent and three of mantissa: 0x1d00ffff is the target 0xffff followed by 26 zero bytes (difficulty 1, the genesis block and chain work 0x100010001), the field 0x1903a30c of block 277,315 gives a difficulty of 1,180,923,195.258, which is the value in the book's listing, and 0x207fffff on the test chain gives the target 7fffff followed by zeros."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_TargetCompactEncoding a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (hex(L.bits_to_target('1d00ffff')), L.difficulty('1903a30c'), L.bits_to_target('207fffff') == int(R['b1_info0']['target'], 16), L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json')['difficulty'], hex(L.work('1d00ffff')), L.has('bitcoinwiki_target.html', '0x00000000FFFF0000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000')) evaluates to ('0xffff0000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000', 1180923195.2580261, True, 1180923195.2580261, '0x100010001', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (hex(L.bits_to_target('1d00ffff')), L.difficulty('1903a30c'), L.bits_to_target('207fffff') == int(R['b1_info0']['target'], 16), L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json')['difficulty'], hex(L.work('1d00ffff')), L.has('bitcoinwiki_target.html', '0x00000000FFFF0000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000'))" ; chx:output "('0xffff0000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000', 1180923195.2580261, True, 1180923195.2580261, '0x100010001', True)" .
chx:X_TargetCompactEncoding rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TargetCompactEncoding .
chx:X_NonceAndExtraNonce a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:NonceAndExtraNonce ; rdfs:label "4.29 billion nonces against 1.18 billion times more work"@en ; skos:definition "The 4-byte nonce offers only 2^32 = 4,294,967,296 values, yet at the difficulty of block 277,315 a block takes about 5 x 10^18 hashes, which is 1,180,941,215 times the nonce space, so miners must change something else as well (the extra nonce in the coinbase, spare version bits, the timestamp); the test chain's blocks needed nonce 1."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_NonceAndExtraNonce a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); d = L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json'); (2 ** 32, d['nonce'], round(L.work('1903a30c') / 2 ** 32), R['b3_block']['json']['nonce'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'extra nonce')) evaluates to (4294967296, 4215469401, 1180941215, 1, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); d = L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json'); (2 ** 32, d['nonce'], round(L.work('1903a30c') / 2 ** 32), R['b3_block']['json']['nonce'], L.has('book_ch12_mining.adoc', 'extra nonce'))" ; chx:output "(4294967296, 4215469401, 1180941215, 1, True)" .
chx:X_NonceAndExtraNonce rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_NonceAndExtraNonce .
chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 ; rdfs:label "SHA-256 applied twice to 80 bytes"@en ; skos:definition "The block hash is the SHA-256 of the SHA-256 of the 80-byte header: the genesis header gives 000000000019d6689c085ae165831e934ff763ae46a2a6c172b3f1b60a8ce26f (displayed byte-reversed), whereas a single SHA-256 gives 6dd6c5716cc8e243 and so on, and the header of block 277,315 hashes to the id that mempool.space lists."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = bytes.fromhex(L.raw('mempool_header_0.txt')); (hashlib.sha256(hashlib.sha256(b).digest()).digest()[::-1].hex() == '000000000019d6689c085ae165831e934ff763ae46a2a6c172b3f1b60a8ce26f', hashlib.sha256(b).digest()[::-1].hex()[:16], L.block_hash(L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt')) == L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json')['id'], L.has('core_src_primitives_block.cpp', 'return (HashWriter{} << *this).GetHash();')) evaluates to (True, '6dd6c5716cc8e243', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = bytes.fromhex(L.raw('mempool_header_0.txt')); (hashlib.sha256(hashlib.sha256(b).digest()).digest()[::-1].hex() == '000000000019d6689c085ae165831e934ff763ae46a2a6c172b3f1b60a8ce26f', hashlib.sha256(b).digest()[::-1].hex()[:16], L.block_hash(L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt')) == L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json')['id'], L.has('core_src_primitives_block.cpp', 'return (HashWriter{} << *this).GetHash();'))" ; chx:output "(True, '6dd6c5716cc8e243', True, True)" .
chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 .
chx:X_HashNotStoredInBlock a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HashNotStoredInBlock ; rdfs:label "the hash is in the next block, not in its own"@en ; skos:definition "A block does not contain its own hash: the 285 bytes of the test chain's genesis block hold neither 0f9188f1... nor its reverse, but the header of block 481 holds the reversed hash of block 480, so the hash is computed on receipt and then stored by the child."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_HashNotStoredInBlock a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = R['b1_genesis']; hs = R['b3_headers_480_489']; (g['hash'] in g['block_hex'], L.rev(g['hash']) in g['block_hex'], L.rev(L.header(hs[0])['hash']) in hs[1], L.header(hs[1])['prev'] == L.header(hs[0])['hash'], len(g['block_hex']) // 2) evaluates to (False, False, True, True, 285)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = R['b1_genesis']; hs = R['b3_headers_480_489']; (g['hash'] in g['block_hex'], L.rev(g['hash']) in g['block_hex'], L.rev(L.header(hs[0])['hash']) in hs[1], L.header(hs[1])['prev'] == L.header(hs[0])['hash'], len(g['block_hex']) // 2)" ; chx:output "(False, False, True, True, 285)" .
chx:X_HashNotStoredInBlock rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HashNotStoredInBlock .
chx:X_HashLeadingZeros a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HashLeadingZeros ; rdfs:label "10, 15 and 19 zero digits"@en ; skos:definition "The long run of zeros in a block hash is a consequence of the target and is not stored: the genesis hash starts with 10 zero hexadecimal digits, block 277,315 with 15 and block 840,000 with 19, each hash is no larger than its target, and the test chain's genesis hash, at the easiest possible target, starts with only 0."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_HashLeadingZeros a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); hs = {n: L.raw('mempool_header_%s.txt' % n) for n in ('0', '277315')}; z = {n: L.leading_zero_hex(L.header(h)['hash']) for n, h in hs.items()}; z['840000'] = L.leading_zero_hex(L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['id']); (z, [int(L.header(h)['hash'], 16) <= L.bits_to_target(L.header(h)['bits']) for h in hs.values()], L.leading_zero_hex(R['b1_genesis']['hash'])) evaluates to ({'0': 10, '277315': 15, '840000': 19}, [True, True], 1)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); hs = {n: L.raw('mempool_header_%s.txt' % n) for n in ('0', '277315')}; z = {n: L.leading_zero_hex(L.header(h)['hash']) for n, h in hs.items()}; z['840000'] = L.leading_zero_hex(L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['id']); (z, [int(L.header(h)['hash'], 16) <= L.bits_to_target(L.header(h)['bits']) for h in hs.values()], L.leading_zero_hex(R['b1_genesis']['hash']))" ; chx:output "({'0': 10, '277315': 15, '840000': 19}, [True, True], 1)" .
chx:X_HashLeadingZeros rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HashLeadingZeros .
chx:X_HeightIsNotUnique a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HeightIsNotUnique ; rdfs:label "two blocks at height 511"@en ; skos:definition "A hash names one block, a height does not: on the test chain two children of the same parent were both at height 511 with different hashes, and the book's tip says so in a box."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_HeightIsNotUnique a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b6_fork']; (f['height1'], f['height2'], f['child1'] != f['child2'], f['prev1'] == f['prev2'] == f['parent'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'does not always identify a single block')) evaluates to (511, 511, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b6_fork']; (f['height1'], f['height2'], f['child1'] != f['child2'], f['prev1'] == f['prev2'] == f['parent'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'does not always identify a single block'))" ; chx:output "(511, 511, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_HeightIsNotUnique rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HeightIsNotUnique .
chx:X_HeightFromGenesis a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HeightFromGenesis ; rdfs:label "971,537 blocks on top of the genesis"@en ; skos:definition "The height counts blocks from the genesis block at height 0: on 2026-10-15 the tip of mainnet was at height 971,537, so 971,538 blocks, 18.5 years at ten minutes each, against the 800,000 that the book reports for mid 2023, and block 840,000 was found on 2024-04-20."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_HeightFromGenesis a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); tip = int(L.raw('mempool_tip_height.txt')); (tip, tip + 1, L.iso(L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['timestamp']), round(tip * 600 / 86400 / 365.25, 1), R['b1_info0']['blocks'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The block height 800,000')) evaluates to (971537, 971538, '2024-04-20 00:09:27', 18.5, 0, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); tip = int(L.raw('mempool_tip_height.txt')); (tip, tip + 1, L.iso(L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json')['timestamp']), round(tip * 600 / 86400 / 365.25, 1), R['b1_info0']['blocks'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The block height 800,000'))" ; chx:output "(971537, 971538, '2024-04-20 00:09:27', 18.5, 0, True)" .
chx:X_HeightFromGenesis rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HeightFromGenesis .
chx:X_Bip34HeightInCoinbase a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip34HeightInCoinbase ; rdfs:label "the height as the first item of the coinbase"@en ; skos:definition "Since BIP 34 the first item of the coinbase script is the height as a minimally encoded number: the test chain's coinbases start 5100 for height 1 (OP_1), 011100 for 17, 02800000 for 128 and 02000100 for 256, which decode back to the heights, and the book calls the purpose that every coinbase differ."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_Bip34HeightInCoinbase a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b3_bip34']; ({h: L.bip34_height(v) for h, v in c.items()} == {h: int(h) for h in c}, c['1'], c['17'], c['128'], c['256'], L.has('bip-0034.mediawiki', 'minimally encoded serialized CScript'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'later protocol change (BIP34)')) evaluates to (True, '5100', '011100', '02800000', '02000100', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b3_bip34']; ({h: L.bip34_height(v) for h, v in c.items()} == {h: int(h) for h in c}, c['1'], c['17'], c['128'], c['256'], L.has('bip-0034.mediawiki', 'minimally encoded serialized CScript'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'later protocol change (BIP34)'))" ; chx:output "(True, '5100', '011100', '02800000', '02000100', True, True)" .
chx:X_Bip34HeightInCoinbase rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip34HeightInCoinbase .
chx:X_CoinbaseMaturity100 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:CoinbaseMaturity100 ; rdfs:label "depth 99 refused, depth 100 allowed"@en ; skos:definition "The reward of a block can be spent only once the block is 100 blocks deep: with COINBASE_MATURITY = 100 the test chain refused a spend at depth 99 with bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase and allowed it at depth 100."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_CoinbaseMaturity100 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = R['b7_maturity']; (L.const('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'COINBASE_MATURITY'), m['confirmations_1']['reject-reason'], m['confirmations_99']['allowed'], m['confirmations_100']['allowed'], m['confirmations_99']['reject-details'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'After 100 blocks back')) evaluates to ('100', 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase', False, True, 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase, tried to spend coinbase at depth 99', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = R['b7_maturity']; (L.const('core_src_consensus_consensus.h', 'COINBASE_MATURITY'), m['confirmations_1']['reject-reason'], m['confirmations_99']['allowed'], m['confirmations_100']['allowed'], m['confirmations_99']['reject-details'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'After 100 blocks back'))" ; chx:output "('100', 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase', False, True, 'bad-txns-premature-spend-of-coinbase, tried to spend coinbase at depth 99', True)" .
chx:X_CoinbaseMaturity100 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_CoinbaseMaturity100 .
chx:X_GenesisHashRecomputed a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GenesisHashRecomputed ; rdfs:label "time 1231006505, nonce 2083236893"@en ; skos:definition "The genesis block can be rebuilt from the numbers in chainparams.cpp, the time 1231006505, the nonce 2083236893, the bits 0x1d00ffff and the message: the 204-byte coinbase gives the transaction id 4a5e1e4b... and the 80-byte header hashes to 000000000019d6689c085ae165831e934ff763ae46a2a6c172b3f1b60a8ce26f."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_GenesisHashRecomputed a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('main'); (g['hash'] == '000000000019d6689c085ae165831e934ff763ae46a2a6c172b3f1b60a8ce26f', g['time'], g['nonce'], g['bits'], g['txid'][:8], g['tx_bytes'], L.header(g['header'])['hash'] == g['hash']) evaluates to (True, 1231006505, 2083236893, '0x1d00ffff', '4a5e1e4b', 204, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('main'); (g['hash'] == '000000000019d6689c085ae165831e934ff763ae46a2a6c172b3f1b60a8ce26f', g['time'], g['nonce'], g['bits'], g['txid'][:8], g['tx_bytes'], L.header(g['header'])['hash'] == g['hash'])" ; chx:output "(True, 1231006505, 2083236893, '0x1d00ffff', '4a5e1e4b', 204, True)" .
chx:X_GenesisHashRecomputed rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GenesisHashRecomputed .
chx:X_GenesisCoinbaseMessage a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GenesisCoinbaseMessage ; rdfs:label "69 characters on 3 January 2009"@en ; skos:definition "The coinbase script of the genesis block holds the 69-character text 'The Times 03/Jan/2009 Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks' after a push of the number 486604799 and a push of the number 4, which proves that the block was not made before that day."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_GenesisCoinbaseMessage a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('main'); (g['message'], len(g['message']), g['scriptsig'][:16], bytes.fromhex(g['scriptsig'])[8:].decode() == g['message'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The Times 03/Jan/2009 Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks.')) evaluates to ('The Times 03/Jan/2009 Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks', 69, '04ffff001d010445', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('main'); (g['message'], len(g['message']), g['scriptsig'][:16], bytes.fromhex(g['scriptsig'])[8:].decode() == g['message'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The Times 03/Jan/2009 Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks.'))" ; chx:output "('The Times 03/Jan/2009 Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks', 69, '04ffff001d010445', True, True)" .
chx:X_GenesisCoinbaseMessage rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GenesisCoinbaseMessage .
chx:X_GenesisHardcoded a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GenesisHardcoded ; rdfs:label "height 0 with no peers"@en ; skos:definition "A node starts with the genesis block built into its code: a Bitcoin Core 31.1 node on the test chain with no peers and no data reported height 0, 0 headers and 293 bytes on disk, and its genesis hash equalled the one rebuilt from chainparams.cpp."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_GenesisHardcoded a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('regtest'); i = R['b1_info0']; (g['hash'] == R['b1_genesis']['hash'], i['blocks'], i['headers'], i['size_on_disk'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'statically encoded within Bitcoin Core')) evaluates to (True, 0, 0, 293, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('regtest'); i = R['b1_info0']; (g['hash'] == R['b1_genesis']['hash'], i['blocks'], i['headers'], i['size_on_disk'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'statically encoded within Bitcoin Core'))" ; chx:output "(True, 0, 0, 293, True)" .
chx:X_GenesisHardcoded rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GenesisHardcoded .
chx:X_GenesisListingMatchesBook a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GenesisListingMatchesBook ; rdfs:label "size 285, weight 1140"@en ; skos:definition "The book's getblock listing of the genesis block agrees with the data of mempool.space in the size 285, the weight 1140, the nonce 2083236893, the bits 1d00ffff (0x1d00ffff), the time 1231006505 and the one transaction, and chain work 0x100010001 is the work of one block at difficulty 1."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_GenesisListingMatchesBook a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_0.json'); (b['size'], b['weight'], b['nonce'], hex(b['bits']), b['timestamp'], b['tx_count'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'nonce' + chr(34) + ': 2083236893'), (chr(34) + 'bits' + chr(34) + ': ' + chr(34) + '1d00ffff' + chr(34)), (chr(34) + 'size' + chr(34) + ': 285'), (chr(34) + 'weight' + chr(34) + ': 1140'), (chr(34) + 'time' + chr(34) + ': 1231006505')), hex(L.work('1d00ffff'))) evaluates to (285, 1140, 2083236893, '0x1d00ffff', 1231006505, 1, True, '0x100010001')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_0.json'); (b['size'], b['weight'], b['nonce'], hex(b['bits']), b['timestamp'], b['tx_count'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'nonce' + chr(34) + ': 2083236893'), (chr(34) + 'bits' + chr(34) + ': ' + chr(34) + '1d00ffff' + chr(34)), (chr(34) + 'size' + chr(34) + ': 285'), (chr(34) + 'weight' + chr(34) + ': 1140'), (chr(34) + 'time' + chr(34) + ': 1231006505')), hex(L.work('1d00ffff')))" ; chx:output "(285, 1140, 2083236893, '0x1d00ffff', 1231006505, 1, True, '0x100010001')" .
chx:X_GenesisListingMatchesBook rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GenesisListingMatchesBook .
chx:X_SharedGenesisTransaction a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SharedGenesisTransaction ; rdfs:label "the same coinbase on four chains"@en ; skos:definition "Mainnet, testnet3, signet and regtest all start from the same 204-byte genesis transaction, id 4a5e1e4b..., and differ only in header (time, nonce, bits), whereas testnet4 has its own coinbase of 180 bytes with id 7aa0a7ae... that carries a different message."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_SharedGenesisTransaction a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ({c: L.chainparams_genesis(c)['txid'][:8] for c in ('main', 'test', 'signet', 'regtest', 'testnet4')}, L.chainparams_genesis('testnet4')['tx_bytes'], L.chainparams_genesis('main')['tx_bytes']) evaluates to ({'main': '4a5e1e4b', 'test': '4a5e1e4b', 'signet': '4a5e1e4b', 'regtest': '4a5e1e4b', 'testnet4': '7aa0a7ae'}, 180, 204)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ({c: L.chainparams_genesis(c)['txid'][:8] for c in ('main', 'test', 'signet', 'regtest', 'testnet4')}, L.chainparams_genesis('testnet4')['tx_bytes'], L.chainparams_genesis('main')['tx_bytes'])" ; chx:output "({'main': '4a5e1e4b', 'test': '4a5e1e4b', 'signet': '4a5e1e4b', 'regtest': '4a5e1e4b', 'testnet4': '7aa0a7ae'}, 180, 204)" .
chx:X_SharedGenesisTransaction rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SharedGenesisTransaction .
chx:X_GenesisCoinbaseUnspendable a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GenesisCoinbaseUnspendable ; rdfs:label "the first 50 BTC that cannot be spent"@en ; skos:definition "The reward of the genesis block cannot be spent: on the test chain getrawtransaction answers that the genesis coinbase is not an ordinary transaction, gettxout finds no output, and the UTXO set at height 0 holds 0 outputs, a quirk that the Bitcoin Wiki says is not known to be intentional."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_GenesisCoinbaseUnspendable a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b1_genesis']; (c['coinbase_getrawtransaction']['error'][:70], c['coinbase_gettxout'], c['txoutsetinfo']['txouts'], L.has('bitcoinwiki_genesis_block.html', ('can' + chr(39) + 't be spent'))) evaluates to ('error code: -5 error message: The genesis block coinbase is not consid', {'ok': ''}, 0, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b1_genesis']; (c['coinbase_getrawtransaction']['error'][:70], c['coinbase_gettxout'], c['txoutsetinfo']['txouts'], L.has('bitcoinwiki_genesis_block.html', ('can' + chr(39) + 't be spent')))" ; chx:output "('error code: -5 error message: The genesis block coinbase is not consid', {'ok': ''}, 0, True)" .
chx:X_GenesisCoinbaseUnspendable rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GenesisCoinbaseUnspendable .
chx:X_ChancellorOfTheHeadline a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ChancellorOfTheHeadline ; rdfs:label "Alistair Darling, 2007 to 2010"@en ; skos:definition "The headline of The Times of 3 January 2009 speaks of the Chancellor, and the Chancellor of the Exchequer then in office was Alistair Darling, who served under Gordon Brown from 2007 to 2010, and The Times began in 1785 as The Daily Universal Register."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_ChancellorOfTheHeadline a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_alistair_darling.html', 'Chancellor of the Exchequer', 'from 2007 to 2010'), L.has('wikipedia_the_times.html', 'It began in 1785 under the title The Daily Universal Register'), L.iso(1231006505)[:10]) evaluates to (True, True, '2009-01-03')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_alistair_darling.html', 'Chancellor of the Exchequer', 'from 2007 to 2010'), L.has('wikipedia_the_times.html', 'It began in 1785 under the title The Daily Universal Register'), L.iso(1231006505)[:10])" ; chx:output "(True, True, '2009-01-03')" .
chx:X_ChancellorOfTheHeadline rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ChancellorOfTheHeadline .
chx:X_PreviousHashPointsToParent a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:PreviousHashPointsToParent ; rdfs:label "9 of 9 links in ten headers"@en ; skos:definition "In ten consecutive headers of the test chain, heights 480 to 489, every header's previous-hash field equalled the recomputed hash of the header before: 9 of 9 links."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_PreviousHashPointsToParent a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = [L.header(h) for h in R['b3_headers_480_489']]; ([p[i]['prev'] == p[i - 1]['hash'] for i in range(1, 10)].count(True), len(p), p[0]['prev'][:8], p[9]['hash'][:8], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'previous block hash' + chr(34)))) evaluates to (9, 10, '45097546', '2576afa6', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = [L.header(h) for h in R['b3_headers_480_489']]; ([p[i]['prev'] == p[i - 1]['hash'] for i in range(1, 10)].count(True), len(p), p[0]['prev'][:8], p[9]['hash'][:8], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'previous block hash' + chr(34))))" ; chx:output "(9, 10, '45097546', '2576afa6', True)" .
chx:X_PreviousHashPointsToParent rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_PreviousHashPointsToParent .
chx:X_Block277315Links a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Block277315Links ; rdfs:label "previous 00000000000000027e7b..."@en ; skos:definition "Block 277,315 of the real chain has the parent hash 00000000000000027e7b... of block 277,314, version 2, time 1388185038, nonce 4215469401 and merkle root 5e049f40..., exactly the values in the book's listing, with 40 transactions in 43,560 bytes and a difficulty of 1180923195.25803."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_Block277315Links a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt')); p = L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277314.txt')); d = L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json'); (h['prev'] == p['hash'] == '00000000000000027e7ba6fe7bad39faf3b5a83daed765f05f7d1b71a1632249', h['hash'] == d['id'], h['version'], h['time'], h['nonce'], h['merkle'][:8], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'nonce' + chr(34) + ' : 4215469401'), (chr(34) + 'time' + chr(34) + ' : 1388185038'), (chr(34) + 'version' + chr(34) + ' : 2'), (chr(34) + 'size' + chr(34) + ' : 43560')), round(L.difficulty(h['bits']), 5), d['size'], d['tx_count']) evaluates to (True, True, 2, 1388185038, 4215469401, '5e049f40', True, 1180923195.25803, 43560, 40)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt')); p = L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277314.txt')); d = L.jload('mempool_block_277315.json'); (h['prev'] == p['hash'] == '00000000000000027e7ba6fe7bad39faf3b5a83daed765f05f7d1b71a1632249', h['hash'] == d['id'], h['version'], h['time'], h['nonce'], h['merkle'][:8], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'nonce' + chr(34) + ' : 4215469401'), (chr(34) + 'time' + chr(34) + ' : 1388185038'), (chr(34) + 'version' + chr(34) + ' : 2'), (chr(34) + 'size' + chr(34) + ' : 43560')), round(L.difficulty(h['bits']), 5), d['size'], d['tx_count'])" ; chx:output "(True, True, 2, 1388185038, 4215469401, '5e049f40', True, 1180923195.25803, 43560, 40)" .
chx:X_Block277315Links rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Block277315Links .
chx:X_TamperingBreaksDescendants a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TamperingBreaksDescendants ; rdfs:label "one flipped bit, seven blocks to redo"@en ; skos:definition "Changing one bit of the merkle root in the header of block 483 of the test chain changed its own hash, so the previous-hash link of block 484 no longer matched, and every one of the 7 blocks from 483 to 489 would have to be mined again."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_TamperingBreaksDescendants a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); hs = R['b3_headers_480_489']; (L.tamper_chain(hs, 3), L.header(hs[3])['hash'][:8]) evaluates to ({'broken_links': [4], 'must_remine': 7, 'own_hash_changed': True}, '373ba4ce')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); hs = R['b3_headers_480_489']; (L.tamper_chain(hs, 3), L.header(hs[3])['hash'][:8])" ; chx:output "({'broken_links': [4], 'must_remine': 7, 'own_hash_changed': True}, '373ba4ce')" .
chx:X_TamperingBreaksDescendants rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TamperingBreaksDescendants .
chx:X_ChainWorkAccumulates a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ChainWorkAccumulates ; rdfs:label "2, 4, 6, 8"@en ; skos:definition "Each header adds its work to the total: on the test chain every block at 0x207fffff adds 2, so chain work was 2, 4, 6 and 8 at heights 0 to 3 and 1002 (0x3ea) after 501 blocks, whereas the genesis block of mainnet starts at 0x100010001."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_ChainWorkAccumulates a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); w = R['b3_chainwork']; ([int(w[str(i)], 16) for i in range(4)], L.work('207fffff'), hex(L.work('1d00ffff')), int(R['b2_info']['chainwork'], 16), 2 * 501) evaluates to ([2, 4, 6, 8], 2, '0x100010001', 1002, 1002)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); w = R['b3_chainwork']; ([int(w[str(i)], 16) for i in range(4)], L.work('207fffff'), hex(L.work('1d00ffff')), int(R['b2_info']['chainwork'], 16), 2 * 501)" ; chx:output "([2, 4, 6, 8], 2, '0x100010001', 1002, 1002)" .
chx:X_ChainWorkAccumulates rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ChainWorkAccumulates .
chx:X_HashChainedTimestamps a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HashChainedTimestamps ; rdfs:label "time-stamping in 1991"@en ; skos:definition "The idea of binding each item to the one before it by a hash is older than Bitcoin: Haber and Stornetta described linked time-stamping of digital documents in 1991, and Nakamoto's paper cites them for the timestamp server."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_HashChainedTimestamps a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('haber_stornetta_1991_timestamp.pdf', 'How To Time-Stamp a Digital Document'), L.has('nakamoto_2008_bitcoin.pdf', 'Haber'), L.has('nakamoto_2008_bitcoin.pdf', 'timestamp server'), L.has('merkle_1980_protocols.pdf', 'tree')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('haber_stornetta_1991_timestamp.pdf', 'How To Time-Stamp a Digital Document'), L.has('nakamoto_2008_bitcoin.pdf', 'Haber'), L.has('nakamoto_2008_bitcoin.pdf', 'timestamp server'), L.has('merkle_1980_protocols.pdf', 'tree'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_HashChainedTimestamps rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HashChainedTimestamps .
chx:X_GlacierCoreAnalogy a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GlacierCoreAnalogy ; rdfs:label "six blocks, an hour of snow"@en ; skos:definition "The book's picture of layers of ice: six blocks are about 60 minutes of topsoil and 100 blocks about 16.7 hours, while ice cores, formed from annual layers of snow, reach back nearly 800,000 years at Dome C, and cores of 2016 from the Allan Hills held ice up to 2.7 million years old."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_GlacierCoreAnalogy a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (6 * 10, round(100 * 10 / 60, 1), L.has('wikipedia_ice_core.html', 'incremental buildup of annual layers of snow'), L.has('wikipedia_ice_core.html', 'going back nearly 800,000 years'), L.has('wikipedia_ice_core.html', '2.7 million'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'glacier core sample')) evaluates to (60, 16.7, True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (6 * 10, round(100 * 10 / 60, 1), L.has('wikipedia_ice_core.html', 'incremental buildup of annual layers of snow'), L.has('wikipedia_ice_core.html', 'going back nearly 800,000 years'), L.has('wikipedia_ice_core.html', '2.7 million'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'glacier core sample'))" ; chx:output "(60, 16.7, True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_GlacierCoreAnalogy rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GlacierCoreAnalogy .
chx:X_TwoChildrenOneParent a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TwoChildrenOneParent ; rdfs:label "two blocks, one parent"@en ; skos:definition "A fork on the test chain: two different blocks with the same parent hash and the same height 511, one active and one a valid-fork branch of length 1."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_TwoChildrenOneParent a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b6_fork']; (f['prev1'] == f['prev2'], f['child1'] != f['child2'], [(t['height'], t['branchlen'], t['status']) for t in f['tips']], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'Each of the children commits to the same parent block')) evaluates to (True, True, [(511, 0, 'active'), (511, 1, 'valid-fork')], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b6_fork']; (f['prev1'] == f['prev2'], f['child1'] != f['child2'], [(t['height'], t['branchlen'], t['status']) for t in f['tips']], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'Each of the children commits to the same parent block'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, [(511, 0, 'active'), (511, 1, 'valid-fork')], True)" .
chx:X_TwoChildrenOneParent rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TwoChildrenOneParent .
chx:X_ForkResolvedByMoreWork a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ForkResolvedByMoreWork ; rdfs:label "the third block decides"@en ; skos:definition "A third block on top of the first child made height 512 the tip, the first child's branch active and the second child a valid-fork branch at height 511 of length 1, so the fork was resolved without anyone deleting a block."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_ForkResolvedByMoreWork a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b6_fork']; (f['extension_prev'] == f['child1'], f['active_is'] == f['extension'], [(t['height'], t['branchlen'], t['status']) for t in f['tips_after']], f['active_before_extension'] == f['child1'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'Eventually only one child block becomes part of the blockchain')) evaluates to (True, True, [(512, 0, 'active'), (511, 1, 'valid-fork')], True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b6_fork']; (f['extension_prev'] == f['child1'], f['active_is'] == f['extension'], [(t['height'], t['branchlen'], t['status']) for t in f['tips_after']], f['active_before_extension'] == f['child1'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'Eventually only one child block becomes part of the blockchain'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, [(512, 0, 'active'), (511, 1, 'valid-fork')], True, True)" .
chx:X_ForkResolvedByMoreWork rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ForkResolvedByMoreWork .
chx:X_ReorgProbabilityFalls a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ReorgProbabilityFalls ; rdfs:label "0.2 for 1 block, 0.0002428 for 6"@en ; skos:definition "Nakamoto's calculation gives the chance that an attacker with 10 percent of the hash rate ever catches up as 1.0, 0.2045873, 0.0509779, 0.0002428 and 0.0000012 when the block is 0, 1, 2, 6 and 10 deep, and 0.1321 for a share of 30 percent at 6 blocks, the numbers behind the book's six topsoil blocks."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_ReorgProbabilityFalls a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ([round(L.catchup(0.1, z), 7) for z in (0, 1, 2, 6, 10)], round(L.catchup(0.3, 6), 4), L.has('nakamoto_2008_bitcoin.pdf', 'z=6 P=0.0002428', 'z=1 P=0.2045873'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The top six blocks are like a few inches of topsoil')) evaluates to ([1.0, 0.2045873, 0.0509779, 0.0002428, 1.2e-06], 0.1321, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ([round(L.catchup(0.1, z), 7) for z in (0, 1, 2, 6, 10)], round(L.catchup(0.3, 6), 4), L.has('nakamoto_2008_bitcoin.pdf', 'z=6 P=0.0002428', 'z=1 P=0.2045873'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The top six blocks are like a few inches of topsoil'))" ; chx:output "([1.0, 0.2045873, 0.0509779, 0.0002428, 1.2e-06], 0.1321, True, True)" .
chx:X_ReorgProbabilityFalls rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ReorgProbabilityFalls .
chx:X_FourLeafTree a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:FourLeafTree ; rdfs:label "three levels, 4 + 2 + 1 hashes"@en ; skos:definition "A block with four transactions has a tree of 4, 2 and 1 hashes: H_AB = SHA256(SHA256(H_A || H_B)) and H_CD likewise, and the double hash of H_AB || H_CD equalled the merkle root in the header of the test chain's block."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_FourLeafTree a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b4_blocks']['4']; ids = b['txids']; i = [bytes.fromhex(t)[::-1] for t in ids]; ab = L.sha256d(i[0] + i[1]); cd = L.sha256d(i[2] + i[3]); lv = L.merkle_levels(ids); ([len(l) for l in lv], L.sha256d(ab + cd)[::-1].hex() == b['merkleroot'], lv[1][0] == ab, L.merkle_root(ids) == L.header(b['header_hex'])['merkle'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'concatenating the two hashes and hashing them together')) evaluates to ([4, 2, 1], True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b4_blocks']['4']; ids = b['txids']; i = [bytes.fromhex(t)[::-1] for t in ids]; ab = L.sha256d(i[0] + i[1]); cd = L.sha256d(i[2] + i[3]); lv = L.merkle_levels(ids); ([len(l) for l in lv], L.sha256d(ab + cd)[::-1].hex() == b['merkleroot'], lv[1][0] == ab, L.merkle_root(ids) == L.header(b['header_hex'])['merkle'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'concatenating the two hashes and hashing them together'))" ; chx:output "([4, 2, 1], True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_FourLeafTree rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_FourLeafTree .
chx:X_OddLeafDuplicated a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:OddLeafDuplicated ; rdfs:label "3 leaves become 4"@en ; skos:definition "With three transactions the third is paired with itself: the tree has 3, 2 and 1 hashes, the root h(h(A||B) || h(C||C)) equalled the header's merkle root, and this rule reproduced the root of all eight test blocks of 1 to 8 transactions."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_OddLeafDuplicated a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b4_blocks']['3']; ids = b['txids']; i = [bytes.fromhex(t)[::-1] for t in ids]; h = L.sha256d; r = h(h(i[0] + i[1]) + h(i[2] + i[2])); ([len(l) for l in L.merkle_levels(ids)], r[::-1].hex() == b['merkleroot'], all(L.merkle_root(R['b4_blocks'][str(n)]['txids']) == R['b4_blocks'][str(n)]['merkleroot'] for n in range(1, 9)), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'the last transaction hash will be duplicated')) evaluates to ([3, 2, 1], True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b4_blocks']['3']; ids = b['txids']; i = [bytes.fromhex(t)[::-1] for t in ids]; h = L.sha256d; r = h(h(i[0] + i[1]) + h(i[2] + i[2])); ([len(l) for l in L.merkle_levels(ids)], r[::-1].hex() == b['merkleroot'], all(L.merkle_root(R['b4_blocks'][str(n)]['txids']) == R['b4_blocks'][str(n)]['merkleroot'] for n in range(1, 9)), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'the last transaction hash will be duplicated'))" ; chx:output "([3, 2, 1], True, True, True)" .
chx:X_OddLeafDuplicated rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_OddLeafDuplicated .
chx:X_RootIsAlways32Bytes a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RootIsAlways32Bytes ; rdfs:label "3,050 transactions, 32 bytes"@en ; skos:definition "The root is 32 bytes whether the block has 1, 2, 8 or 16 transactions or the 3,050 of block 840,000, and with one transaction the root is that transaction's id, as in the genesis block."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_RootIsAlways32Bytes a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); bs = R['b4_blocks']; g = L.jload('mempool_block_0.json'); m = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json'); ([(n, len(bytes.fromhex(L.header(bs[str(n)]['header_hex'])['merkle']))) for n in (1, 2, 8, 16)], bs['1']['merkleroot'] == bs['1']['txids'][0], L.chainparams_genesis('main')['txid'] == g['merkle_root'], len(m['merkle_root']) // 2, m['tx_count']) evaluates to ([(1, 32), (2, 32), (8, 32), (16, 32)], True, True, 32, 3050)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); bs = R['b4_blocks']; g = L.jload('mempool_block_0.json'); m = L.jload('mempool_block_840000.json'); ([(n, len(bytes.fromhex(L.header(bs[str(n)]['header_hex'])['merkle']))) for n in (1, 2, 8, 16)], bs['1']['merkleroot'] == bs['1']['txids'][0], L.chainparams_genesis('main')['txid'] == g['merkle_root'], len(m['merkle_root']) // 2, m['tx_count'])" ; chx:output "([(1, 32), (2, 32), (8, 32), (16, 32)], True, True, 32, 3050)" .
chx:X_RootIsAlways32Bytes rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RootIsAlways32Bytes .
chx:X_TreeDepth a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TreeDepth ; rdfs:label "ceiling of log2 N"@en ; skos:definition "The depth of the tree is the ceiling of log2 of the number of leaves: 0 for 1 transaction, 2 for 4, 4 for 16, 6 for the 40 transactions of block 277,315, 12 for the 3,050 of block 840,000 and 14 for 16,000."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_TreeDepth a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ids = L.jload('mempool_txids_277315.json'); ([(n, L.depth(n)) for n in (1, 2, 3, 4, 16, 40, 3050, 16000)], len(L.merkle_levels(ids)) - 1, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'about +log~2~(N)+ calculations')) evaluates to ([(1, 0), (2, 1), (3, 2), (4, 2), (16, 4), (40, 6), (3050, 12), (16000, 14)], 6, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ids = L.jload('mempool_txids_277315.json'); ([(n, L.depth(n)) for n in (1, 2, 3, 4, 16, 40, 3050, 16000)], len(L.merkle_levels(ids)) - 1, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'about +log~2~(N)+ calculations'))" ; chx:output "([(1, 0), (2, 1), (3, 2), (4, 2), (16, 4), (40, 6), (3050, 12), (16000, 14)], 6, True)" .
chx:X_TreeDepth rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TreeDepth .
chx:X_RealBlockRoot a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RealBlockRoot ; rdfs:label "40 txids of block 277,315"@en ; skos:definition "From the 40 transaction ids of block 277,315, 257e7497... to 05cfd38f..., the code reproduces the merkle root 5e049f40... that the block header and the book give."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_RealBlockRoot a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ids = L.jload('mempool_txids_277315.json'); (len(ids), L.merkle_root(ids) == L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt'))['merkle'], ids[0][:8], ids[-1][:8], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', ids[0], ids[-1])) evaluates to (40, True, '257e7497', '05cfd38f', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ids = L.jload('mempool_txids_277315.json'); (len(ids), L.merkle_root(ids) == L.header(L.raw('mempool_header_277315.txt'))['merkle'], ids[0][:8], ids[-1][:8], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', ids[0], ids[-1]))" ; chx:output "(40, True, '257e7497', '05cfd38f', True)" .
chx:X_RealBlockRoot rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RealBlockRoot .
chx:X_HashTreeHistory a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HashTreeHistory ; rdfs:label "patented in 1979"@en ; skos:definition "The hash tree is named after Ralph Merkle, who patented it in 1979 (US patent 4309569 of 1982) and described it for public-key protocols in a paper of 1980."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_HashTreeHistory a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_merkle_tree.html', 'who patented it in 1979'), L.has('wikipedia_merkle_tree.html', 'patent 4309569'), L.has('wikipedia_ralph_merkle.html', 'Merkle'), L.has('merkle_1980_protocols.pdf', 'Ralph C. Merkle', 'ELXSi International')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_merkle_tree.html', 'who patented it in 1979'), L.has('wikipedia_merkle_tree.html', 'patent 4309569'), L.has('wikipedia_ralph_merkle.html', 'Merkle'), L.has('merkle_1980_protocols.pdf', 'Ralph C. Merkle', 'ELXSi International'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_HashTreeHistory rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HashTreeHistory .
chx:X_Cve20122459Trees a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Cve20122459Trees ; rdfs:label "[1..6] and [1..6,5,6]"@en ; skos:definition "The lists of six and of eight transaction ids [1,2,3,4,5,6] and [1,2,3,4,5,6,5,6] have the same merkle root, and so do [1,2,3] and [1,2,3,3], but [1,2,3,4] and [1,2,3,4,3,4] do not: the duplication of an odd last hash can be forged."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_Cve20122459Trees a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ids = [L.sha256d(bytes([i])).hex() for i in range(1, 7)]; b = ids + [ids[4], ids[5]]; (L.merkle_root(ids) == L.merkle_root(b), len(ids), len(b), L.merkle_root(ids[:3]) == L.merkle_root(ids[:3] + [ids[2]]), L.merkle_root(ids[:4]) == L.merkle_root(ids[:4] + ids[2:4]), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '[1,2,3,4,5,6] and [1,2,3,4,5,6,5,6]')) evaluates to (True, 6, 8, True, False, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ids = [L.sha256d(bytes([i])).hex() for i in range(1, 7)]; b = ids + [ids[4], ids[5]]; (L.merkle_root(ids) == L.merkle_root(b), len(ids), len(b), L.merkle_root(ids[:3]) == L.merkle_root(ids[:3] + [ids[2]]), L.merkle_root(ids[:4]) == L.merkle_root(ids[:4] + ids[2:4]), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '[1,2,3,4,5,6] and [1,2,3,4,5,6,5,6]'))" ; chx:output "(True, 6, 8, True, False, True)" .
chx:X_Cve20122459Trees rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Cve20122459Trees .
chx:X_NodeRejectsMutatedBlock a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:NodeRejectsMutatedBlock ; rdfs:label "bad-txns-duplicate, then the real block"@en ; skos:definition "A block of 3 transactions was changed into one of 4 by repeating the last transaction, with the same header and the same hash: submitblock answered bad-txns-duplicate, and the original block was then accepted and became the tip, so the invalid form did not block the valid one."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_NodeRejectsMutatedBlock a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = R['b5_mutation']; (m['n_original'], m['n_mutated'], m['same_header'], m['submit_mutated'], m['submit_original'], m['tip_is_original']) evaluates to (3, 4, True, {'ok': 'bad-txns-duplicate'}, {'ok': ''}, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = R['b5_mutation']; (m['n_original'], m['n_mutated'], m['same_header'], m['submit_mutated'], m['submit_original'], m['tip_is_original'])" ; chx:output "(3, 4, True, {'ok': 'bad-txns-duplicate'}, {'ok': ''}, True)" .
chx:X_NodeRejectsMutatedBlock rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_NodeRejectsMutatedBlock .
chx:X_MutationDefenseInSource a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MutationDefenseInSource ; rdfs:label "comment in merkle.cpp"@en ; skos:definition "Bitcoin Core's merkle.cpp warns of CVE-2012-2459 and reports a mutated block, validation.cpp rejects it as bad-txns-duplicate (the run showed the genuine block accepted afterwards), and Optech dates the report to 2012 and a variation to version 0.13.0 of 2016."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_MutationDefenseInSource a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('core_src_consensus_merkle.cpp', 'CVE-2012-2459', 'mutated'), L.has('core_src_validation.cpp', 'bad-txns-duplicate'), L.has('optech_topic_merkle_tree_vulnerabilities.html', 'The vulnerability was reported in 2012'), L.has('optech_topic_merkle_tree_vulnerabilities.html', 'version 0.13.0 (2016)')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('core_src_consensus_merkle.cpp', 'CVE-2012-2459', 'mutated'), L.has('core_src_validation.cpp', 'bad-txns-duplicate'), L.has('optech_topic_merkle_tree_vulnerabilities.html', 'The vulnerability was reported in 2012'), L.has('optech_topic_merkle_tree_vulnerabilities.html', 'version 0.13.0 (2016)'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_MutationDefenseInSource rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MutationDefenseInSource .
chx:X_SixtyFourByteWeakness a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SixtyFourByteWeakness ; rdfs:label "an inner node is 64 bytes"@en ; skos:definition "An inner node is the hash of 64 bytes, two hashes joined, and a transaction can be exactly 64 bytes without witness data (the smallest is 60), so it can be mistaken for an inner node, the weakness of CVE-2017-12842 that BIP 54 closes by making such transactions invalid."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_SixtyFourByteWeakness a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ids = R['b4_blocks']['4']['txids']; inner = bytes.fromhex(ids[0])[::-1] + bytes.fromhex(ids[1])[::-1]; (len(inner), 240 // 4, L.has('bip-0054.md', 'Transactions whose witness-stripped serialized size is exactly 64 bytes are invalid'), L.has('optech_topic_merkle_tree_vulnerabilities.html', 'CVE-2017-12842')) evaluates to (64, 60, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ids = R['b4_blocks']['4']['txids']; inner = bytes.fromhex(ids[0])[::-1] + bytes.fromhex(ids[1])[::-1]; (len(inner), 240 // 4, L.has('bip-0054.md', 'Transactions whose witness-stripped serialized size is exactly 64 bytes are invalid'), L.has('optech_topic_merkle_tree_vulnerabilities.html', 'CVE-2017-12842'))" ; chx:output "(64, 60, True, True)" .
chx:X_SixtyFourByteWeakness rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SixtyFourByteWeakness .
chx:X_MerklePathOf16 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MerklePathOf16 ; rdfs:label "K of 16: L, IJ, MNOP, ABCDEFGH"@en ; skos:definition "For the 11th of 16 transactions (index 10, the K of the book's figure) the path has 4 hashes, 128 bytes, with the siblings on the right, left, right and left, and following it gave the merkle root of the test chain's 16-transaction block."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_MerklePathOf16 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b4_blocks']['16']; ids = b['txids']; p = L.merkle_path(ids, 10); (len(p), 32 * len(p), [r for s, r in p], L.follow_path(ids[10], p) == b['merkleroot'], ids[10] == R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['txid'], R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['index'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'only four 32-byte hashes long (128 bytes total)')) evaluates to (4, 128, [True, False, True, False], True, True, 10, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b4_blocks']['16']; ids = b['txids']; p = L.merkle_path(ids, 10); (len(p), 32 * len(p), [r for s, r in p], L.follow_path(ids[10], p) == b['merkleroot'], ids[10] == R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['txid'], R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['index'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'only four 32-byte hashes long (128 bytes total)'))" ; chx:output "(4, 128, [True, False, True, False], True, True, 10, True)" .
chx:X_MerklePathOf16 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MerklePathOf16 .
chx:X_PathLengthLogarithm a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:PathLengthLogarithm ; rdfs:label "10 to 14 hashes"@en ; skos:definition "A path for 1,024 transactions has 10 hashes (320 bytes), for 4,096 has 12 (384 bytes) and for 16,000 has 14 (448 bytes), and block 277,315 with 40 transactions needs 6."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_PathLengthLogarithm a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ([(n, L.depth(n), 32 * L.depth(n)) for n in (1024, 4096, 16000)], len(L.merkle_path(L.jload('mempool_txids_277315.json'), 7)), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'paths of 10 or 12 hashes (320–384 bytes)')) evaluates to ([(1024, 10, 320), (4096, 12, 384), (16000, 14, 448)], 6, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ([(n, L.depth(n), 32 * L.depth(n)) for n in (1024, 4096, 16000)], len(L.merkle_path(L.jload('mempool_txids_277315.json'), 7)), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'paths of 10 or 12 hashes (320–384 bytes)'))" ; chx:output "([(1024, 10, 320), (4096, 12, 384), (16000, 14, 448)], 6, True)" .
chx:X_PathLengthLogarithm rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_PathLengthLogarithm .
chx:X_ProofSizeVsBlock a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ProofSizeVsBlock ; rdfs:label "7,576 times, not 10,000"@en ; skos:definition "A proof of 80 + 448 = 528 bytes is 7,576 times smaller than a block of 4,000,000 bytes, and with a typical 250-byte transaction added 5,141 times smaller, so the book's 'almost 10,000 times' would need a proof of 400 bytes."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_ProofSizeVsBlock a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (round(4000000 / (80 + 448)), round(4000000 / (250 + 80 + 448)), 4000000 // 10000, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'almost 10,000 times smaller')) evaluates to (7576, 5141, 400, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (round(4000000 / (80 + 448)), round(4000000 / (250 + 80 + 448)), 4000000 // 10000, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'almost 10,000 times smaller'))" ; chx:output "(7576, 5141, 400, True)" .
chx:X_ProofSizeVsBlock rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ProofSizeVsBlock .
chx:X_MerkleblockForLightClients a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MerkleblockForLightClients ; rdfs:label "248 bytes against 3,580"@en ; skos:definition "The merkleblock that Bitcoin Core made for one transaction of the test chain's 16-transaction block was 248 bytes (header, count 16, 5 hashes, flags) against the block's 3,580 bytes, and verifytxoutproof returned the transaction; for a block of 4 transactions it was 183 bytes."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_MerkleblockForLightClients a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = L.parse_merkleblock(R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['proof_hex']); q = L.parse_merkleblock(R['b4_proof_for_third_of_4']['proof_hex']); (p['total'], p['ntx'], len(p['hashes']), q['total'], q['ntx'], len(q['hashes']), p['header'] == R['b4_blocks']['16']['header_hex'], R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['verify'] == [R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['txid']], R['b4_blocks']['16']['size'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'less than a kilobyte of data')) evaluates to (248, 16, 5, 183, 4, 3, True, True, 3580, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = L.parse_merkleblock(R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['proof_hex']); q = L.parse_merkleblock(R['b4_proof_for_third_of_4']['proof_hex']); (p['total'], p['ntx'], len(p['hashes']), q['total'], q['ntx'], len(q['hashes']), p['header'] == R['b4_blocks']['16']['header_hex'], R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['verify'] == [R['b4_proof_for_k_of_16']['txid']], R['b4_blocks']['16']['size'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'less than a kilobyte of data'))" ; chx:output "(248, 16, 5, 183, 4, 3, True, True, 3580, True)" .
chx:X_MerkleblockForLightClients rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MerkleblockForLightClients .
chx:X_MerkleProofDirection a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MerkleProofDirection ; rdfs:label "left and right matter"@en ; skos:definition "The order of every pair matters: following the path with the right sides swapped did not give the root, and the sides are the bits of the transaction's position, 1010 read from the lowest bit for index 10."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_MerkleProofDirection a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b4_blocks']['16']; ids = b['txids']; p = L.merkle_path(ids, 10); (L.follow_path(ids[10], p) == b['merkleroot'], L.follow_path(ids[10], p, swap=True) == b['merkleroot'], [int(c) for c in bin(10)[2:].zfill(4)][::-1], [int(not r) for s, r in p]) evaluates to (True, False, [0, 1, 0, 1], [0, 1, 0, 1])"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b4_blocks']['16']; ids = b['txids']; p = L.merkle_path(ids, 10); (L.follow_path(ids[10], p) == b['merkleroot'], L.follow_path(ids[10], p, swap=True) == b['merkleroot'], [int(c) for c in bin(10)[2:].zfill(4)][::-1], [int(not r) for s, r in p])" ; chx:output "(True, False, [0, 1, 0, 1], [0, 1, 0, 1])" .
chx:X_MerkleProofDirection rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MerkleProofDirection .
chx:X_SeveralChainsExist a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SeveralChainsExist ; rdfs:label "five chains, five genesis blocks"@en ; skos:definition "Bitcoin Core 31.1 knows five chains, main, test, testnet4, signet and regtest, and the genesis hashes that the nodes reported for testnet3, testnet4, signet and regtest equal those rebuilt from chainparams.cpp."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_SeveralChainsExist a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; (all(L.chainparams_genesis(a)['hash'] == c[b]['genesis_hash'] for a, b in (('test', 'testnet3_option'), ('testnet4', 'testnet4'), ('signet', 'signet'))), L.chainparams_genesis('regtest')['hash'] == R['b1_genesis']['hash'], sorted(c), L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', 'testnet4, signet, regtest'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'at this time _testnet_, _signet_, and _regtest_')) evaluates to (True, True, ['custom_signet', 'signet', 'testnet3_option', 'testnet4'], True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; (all(L.chainparams_genesis(a)['hash'] == c[b]['genesis_hash'] for a, b in (('test', 'testnet3_option'), ('testnet4', 'testnet4'), ('signet', 'signet'))), L.chainparams_genesis('regtest')['hash'] == R['b1_genesis']['hash'], sorted(c), L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', 'testnet4, signet, regtest'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'at this time _testnet_, _signet_, and _regtest_'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, ['custom_signet', 'signet', 'testnet3_option', 'testnet4'], True, True)" .
chx:X_SeveralChainsExist rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SeveralChainsExist .
chx:X_AddressPrefixes a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:AddressPrefixes ; rdfs:label "m, 2, tb1 and bcrt1"@en ; skos:definition "The test chains share the base58 prefixes 111 (addresses starting m or n) and 196 (starting 2) and the bech32 prefix tb, with tb1q for segwit and tb1p for taproot, while regtest uses bcrt1q and bcrt1p, so the book's list of m, n and tb1 leaves out the 2 and the regtest prefix that its own listing uses."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_AddressPrefixes a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = lambda a: (a['legacy'][0], a['p2sh-segwit'][0], a['bech32'][:a['bech32'].index('1') + 2], a['bech32m'][:a['bech32m'].index('1') + 2]); c = R['b9_chains']; ({'regtest': f(R['b8_regtest_addresses']), 'testnet4': f(c['testnet4']['addresses']), 'signet': f(c['signet']['addresses'])}, [(k, L.chain_facts(k)['p2pkh'], L.chain_facts(k)['p2sh'], L.chain_facts(k)['hrp']) for k in ('main', 'test', 'regtest')], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'begin with +m+, +n+, or +tb1+')) evaluates to ({'regtest': ('m', '2', 'bcrt1q', 'bcrt1p'), 'testnet4': ('m', '2', 'tb1q', 'tb1p'), 'signet': ('m', '2', 'tb1q', 'tb1p')}, [('main', 0, 5, 'bc'), ('test', 111, 196, 'tb'), ('regtest', 111, 196, 'bcrt')], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = lambda a: (a['legacy'][0], a['p2sh-segwit'][0], a['bech32'][:a['bech32'].index('1') + 2], a['bech32m'][:a['bech32m'].index('1') + 2]); c = R['b9_chains']; ({'regtest': f(R['b8_regtest_addresses']), 'testnet4': f(c['testnet4']['addresses']), 'signet': f(c['signet']['addresses'])}, [(k, L.chain_facts(k)['p2pkh'], L.chain_facts(k)['p2sh'], L.chain_facts(k)['hrp']) for k in ('main', 'test', 'regtest')], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'begin with +m+, +n+, or +tb1+'))" ; chx:output "({'regtest': ('m', '2', 'bcrt1q', 'bcrt1p'), 'testnet4': ('m', '2', 'tb1q', 'tb1p'), 'signet': ('m', '2', 'tb1q', 'tb1p')}, [('main', 0, 5, 'bc'), ('test', 111, 196, 'tb'), ('regtest', 111, 196, 'bcrt')], True)" .
chx:X_AddressPrefixes rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_AddressPrefixes .
chx:X_DataDirectories a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:DataDirectories ; rdfs:label "testnet3, testnet4, signet, regtest"@en ; skos:definition "Each chain keeps its data in its own subdirectory, regtest, testnet3, testnet4 and signet, and uses its own port: 8333, 18333, 48333, 38333 and 18444."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_DataDirectories a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; (R['b1_datadir'], c['testnet4']['datadir'], c['signet']['datadir'], c['testnet3_option']['datadir'], [L.chain_facts(k)['port'] for k in ('main', 'test', 'testnet4', 'signet', 'regtest')], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '+testnet3+ subdirectory')) evaluates to (['regtest'], ['testnet4'], ['signet'], ['testnet3'], [8333, 18333, 48333, 38333, 18444], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; (R['b1_datadir'], c['testnet4']['datadir'], c['signet']['datadir'], c['testnet3_option']['datadir'], [L.chain_facts(k)['port'] for k in ('main', 'test', 'testnet4', 'signet', 'regtest')], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '+testnet3+ subdirectory'))" ; chx:output "(['regtest'], ['testnet4'], ['signet'], ['testnet3'], [8333, 18333, 48333, 38333, 18444], True)" .
chx:X_DataDirectories rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_DataDirectories .
chx:X_AssumedChainSizes a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:AssumedChainSizes ; rdfs:label "245 GB for testnet3, 24 GB for signet"@en ; skos:definition "Bitcoin Core's own estimate of the disk space of each chain, kept in chainparams.cpp for the free-space warning, is 856 GB for mainnet, 245 GB for testnet3, 31 GB for testnet4 and 24 GB for the default signet, which makes testnet3 about 8 times the book's 'in excess of 30 GB' and the signet 31 times the 769,525,915 bytes of the book's listing."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_AssumedChainSizes a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = {k: L.chain_facts(k)['assumed_gb'] for k in ('main', 'test', 'testnet4', 'signet', 'regtest')}; (f, round(f['test'] / 30, 1), round(f['signet'] * 1e9 / 769525915, 1), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'in excess of 30 GB in 2023'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'size_on_disk' + chr(34) + ': 769525915'))) evaluates to ({'main': 856, 'test': 245, 'testnet4': 31, 'signet': 24, 'regtest': 0}, 8.2, 31.2, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = {k: L.chain_facts(k)['assumed_gb'] for k in ('main', 'test', 'testnet4', 'signet', 'regtest')}; (f, round(f['test'] / 30, 1), round(f['signet'] * 1e9 / 769525915, 1), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'in excess of 30 GB in 2023'), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'size_on_disk' + chr(34) + ': 769525915')))" ; chx:output "({'main': 856, 'test': 245, 'testnet4': 31, 'signet': 24, 'regtest': 0}, 8.2, 31.2, True, True)" .
chx:X_AssumedChainSizes rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_AssumedChainSizes .
chx:X_Testnet3StillThere a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Testnet3StillThere ; rdfs:label "testnet3 at block 5,189,394"@en ; skos:definition "Bitcoin Core 31.1 still starts testnet3 with -testnet (chain name test, directory testnet3), though the help text says the support is deprecated and will be removed, and the chain created on 2011-02-02 stood on 2026-10-15 at height 5,189,394."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_Testnet3StillThere a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']['testnet3_option']; (c['info']['chain'], c['datadir'], L.iso(c['info']['time'])[:10], L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', 'Support for testnet3 is deprecated and will be removed in an upcoming release'), int(L.raw('mempool_testnet3_tip_height.txt')), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The current testnet is called _testnet3_')) evaluates to ('test', ['testnet3'], '2011-02-02', True, 5189394, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']['testnet3_option']; (c['info']['chain'], c['datadir'], L.iso(c['info']['time'])[:10], L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', 'Support for testnet3 is deprecated and will be removed in an upcoming release'), int(L.raw('mempool_testnet3_tip_height.txt')), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'The current testnet is called _testnet3_'))" ; chx:output "('test', ['testnet3'], '2011-02-02', True, 5189394, True)" .
chx:X_Testnet3StillThere rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Testnet3StillThere .
chx:X_Testnet4Replaces a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Testnet4Replaces ; rdfs:label "genesis 03/May/2024"@en ; skos:definition "Testnet4 begins with a genesis block that quotes the Bitcoin block hash of 3 May 2024, hash 00000000da84f2ba..., time 2024-05-03 23:11:00 UTC, added to Bitcoin Core in release 28.0 by BIP 94, and it stood on 2026-10-15 at height 156,618."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_Testnet4Replaces a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('testnet4'); (g['hash'][:16], g['message'], L.iso(g['time']), int(L.raw('mempool_testnet4_tip_height.txt')), L.has('core_relnotes_28.0.md', 'Support for Testnet4 as specified in'), L.has('bip-0094.mediawiki', 'Status: Deployed')) evaluates to ('00000000da84f2ba', '03/May/2024 000000000000000000001ebd58c244970b3aa9d783bb001011fbe8ea8e98e00e', '2024-05-03 23:11:00', 156618, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.chainparams_genesis('testnet4'); (g['hash'][:16], g['message'], L.iso(g['time']), int(L.raw('mempool_testnet4_tip_height.txt')), L.has('core_relnotes_28.0.md', 'Support for Testnet4 as specified in'), L.has('bip-0094.mediawiki', 'Status: Deployed'))" ; chx:output "('00000000da84f2ba', '03/May/2024 000000000000000000001ebd58c244970b3aa9d783bb001011fbe8ea8e98e00e', '2024-05-03 23:11:00', 156618, True, True)" .
chx:X_Testnet4Replaces rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Testnet4Replaces .
chx:X_TestnetMinimumDifficulty a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TestnetMinimumDifficulty ; rdfs:label "20 minutes, not half"@en ; skos:definition "The code lets testnet3, testnet4 and regtest (not mainnet, not signet) mine a block at the minimum difficulty when its time is more than 2 x 10 = 20 minutes after the previous block; the book's 'half that of Bitcoin' does not show in the code, in which mainnet and testnet3 have the same limit 00000000ffff....."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_TestnetMinimumDifficulty a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = {k: L.chain_facts(k) for k in ('main', 'test', 'testnet4', 'signet', 'regtest')}; (f['main']['powlimit'] == f['test']['powlimit'], {k: v['min_diff'] for k, v in f.items()}, L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'pindexLast->GetBlockTime() + params.nPowTargetSpacing*2'), 2 * 600 // 60, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'its minimum difficulty is half that of Bitcoin'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_testnet.html', 'equal to difficulty of 0.5 on mainnet')) evaluates to (True, {'main': False, 'test': True, 'testnet4': True, 'signet': False, 'regtest': True}, True, 20, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = {k: L.chain_facts(k) for k in ('main', 'test', 'testnet4', 'signet', 'regtest')}; (f['main']['powlimit'] == f['test']['powlimit'], {k: v['min_diff'] for k, v in f.items()}, L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'pindexLast->GetBlockTime() + params.nPowTargetSpacing*2'), 2 * 600 // 60, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'its minimum difficulty is half that of Bitcoin'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_testnet.html', 'equal to difficulty of 0.5 on mainnet'))" ; chx:output "(True, {'main': False, 'test': True, 'testnet4': True, 'signet': False, 'regtest': True}, True, 20, True, True)" .
chx:X_TestnetMinimumDifficulty rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TestnetMinimumDifficulty .
chx:X_TestnetBlockStorms a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TestnetBlockStorms ; rdfs:label "5.2 million blocks in 15.7 years"@en ; skos:definition "Testnet3 has 5,189,394 blocks, 6.3 times the 825,696 that ten-minute blocks would have given since 2011-02-02, and more than 5 times mainnet's 971,537, because the minimum-difficulty rule lets a miner mine in bursts."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_TestnetBlockStorms a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = int(L.raw('mempool_testnet3_tip_height.txt')); d = (datetime.datetime(2026, 10, 15) - datetime.datetime(2011, 2, 2)).days; (n, d * 144, round(n / (d * 144), 1), int(L.raw('mempool_tip_height.txt')), L.has('bip-0094.mediawiki', ('three years' + chr(39) + ' worth of blocks were mined in a few weeks'))) evaluates to (5189394, 825696, 6.3, 971537, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = int(L.raw('mempool_testnet3_tip_height.txt')); d = (datetime.datetime(2026, 10, 15) - datetime.datetime(2011, 2, 2)).days; (n, d * 144, round(n / (d * 144), 1), int(L.raw('mempool_tip_height.txt')), L.has('bip-0094.mediawiki', ('three years' + chr(39) + ' worth of blocks were mined in a few weeks')))" ; chx:output "(5189394, 825696, 6.3, 971537, True)" .
chx:X_TestnetBlockStorms rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TestnetBlockStorms .
chx:X_Bip94Rules a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip94Rules ; rdfs:label "timewarp bound of 600 seconds"@en ; skos:definition "BIP 94 changes two rules for testnet4: the retarget starts from the first block of the previous period, and the first block of a period may be no more than 600 seconds earlier than its parent; the code switches this on with enforce_BIP94, which only testnet4 sets, and release 29.0 switched the timewarp rule off for regtest."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_Bip94Rules a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'if (params.enforce_BIP94)', 'pindexFirst->nBits'), {k: L.chain_facts(k)['bip94'] for k in ('main', 'test', 'testnet4', 'signet', 'regtest')}, L.has('bip-0094.mediawiki', 'minus 600 seconds'), L.has('core_relnotes_29.0.md', 'The BIP94 timewarp attack mitigation (designed for testnet4) is no longer active on the regtest network')) evaluates to (True, {'main': 'false', 'test': 'false', 'testnet4': 'true', 'signet': 'false', 'regtest': 'opts.enforce_bip94'}, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('core_src_pow.cpp', 'if (params.enforce_BIP94)', 'pindexFirst->nBits'), {k: L.chain_facts(k)['bip94'] for k in ('main', 'test', 'testnet4', 'signet', 'regtest')}, L.has('bip-0094.mediawiki', 'minus 600 seconds'), L.has('core_relnotes_29.0.md', 'The BIP94 timewarp attack mitigation (designed for testnet4) is no longer active on the regtest network'))" ; chx:output "(True, {'main': 'false', 'test': 'false', 'testnet4': 'true', 'signet': 'false', 'regtest': 'opts.enforce_bip94'}, True, True)" .
chx:X_Bip94Rules rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip94Rules .
chx:X_SignetChallengeIsMultisig a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SignetChallengeIsMultisig ; rdfs:label "1 of 2 keys"@en ; skos:definition "The default signet's challenge is a 71-byte script, OP_1 followed by two 33-byte keys and OP_2 OP_CHECKMULTISIG, so a block needs the signature of one of the two operators, while the custom signet of the run used the one-byte challenge 51 (OP_1), which anyone can satisfy."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_SignetChallengeIsMultisig a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; ch = c['signet']['info']['signet_challenge']; (L.script_ops(ch), len(ch) // 2, L.script_ops(c['custom_signet']['info']['signet_challenge']), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'operated by two contributors'), L.has('bip-0325.mediawiki', 'challenge')) evaluates to (['OP_1', 'PUSH33', 'PUSH33', 'OP_2', 'OP_CHECKMULTISIG'], 71, ['OP_1'], True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; ch = c['signet']['info']['signet_challenge']; (L.script_ops(ch), len(ch) // 2, L.script_ops(c['custom_signet']['info']['signet_challenge']), L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'operated by two contributors'), L.has('bip-0325.mediawiki', 'challenge'))" ; chx:output "(['OP_1', 'PUSH33', 'PUSH33', 'OP_2', 'OP_CHECKMULTISIG'], 71, ['OP_1'], True, True)" .
chx:X_SignetChallengeIsMultisig rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SignetChallengeIsMultisig .
chx:X_SignetMagicFromChallenge a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SignetMagicFromChallenge ; rdfs:label "0a03cf40 for the default signet"@en ; skos:definition "The four message-start bytes of a signet are the first four bytes of the double SHA-256 of its challenge: 0a03cf40 for the default signet, 54d26fbd for the challenge 51, and 7ec653a5 for the example of BIP 325, so two signets do not talk to each other by mistake."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_SignetMagicFromChallenge a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; ch = c['signet']['info']['signet_challenge']; (L.signet_magic(ch), L.signet_magic('51'), L.signet_magic('512103ad5e0edad18cb1f0fc0d28a3d4f1f3e445640337489abb10404f2d1e086be430210359ef5021964fe22d6f8e05b2463c9540ce96883fe3b278760f048f5189f2e6c452ae') == L.signet_magic(ch), L.has('bip-0325.mediawiki', 'First four bytes = the message start = 7ec653a5'), L.has('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', 'message start is defined as the first 4 bytes of the sha256d of the block script')) evaluates to ('0a03cf40', '54d26fbd', True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; ch = c['signet']['info']['signet_challenge']; (L.signet_magic(ch), L.signet_magic('51'), L.signet_magic('512103ad5e0edad18cb1f0fc0d28a3d4f1f3e445640337489abb10404f2d1e086be430210359ef5021964fe22d6f8e05b2463c9540ce96883fe3b278760f048f5189f2e6c452ae') == L.signet_magic(ch), L.has('bip-0325.mediawiki', 'First four bytes = the message start = 7ec653a5'), L.has('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', 'message start is defined as the first 4 bytes of the sha256d of the block script'))" ; chx:output "('0a03cf40', '54d26fbd', True, True, True)" .
chx:X_SignetMagicFromChallenge rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SignetMagicFromChallenge .
chx:X_SignetGenesisShared a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SignetGenesisShared ; rdfs:label "the same genesis for every signet"@en ; skos:definition "The default signet and the custom signet with the challenge 51 have the same genesis block 000000088198..., time 2020-09-01 00:00:00 UTC and bits 1e0377ae, because the genesis does not contain the challenge."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_SignetGenesisShared a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; (c['signet']['genesis_hash'] == c['custom_signet']['genesis_hash'], c['signet']['genesis_hash'][:12], L.iso(c['signet']['info']['time']), c['signet']['info']['bits'], c['signet']['info']['signet_challenge'] != c['custom_signet']['info']['signet_challenge'], L.chainparams_genesis('signet')['hash'] == c['signet']['genesis_hash']) evaluates to (True, '000000088198', '2020-09-01 00:00:00', '1e0377ae', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b9_chains']; (c['signet']['genesis_hash'] == c['custom_signet']['genesis_hash'], c['signet']['genesis_hash'][:12], L.iso(c['signet']['info']['time']), c['signet']['info']['bits'], c['signet']['info']['signet_challenge'] != c['custom_signet']['info']['signet_challenge'], L.chainparams_genesis('signet')['hash'] == c['signet']['genesis_hash'])" ; chx:output "(True, '000000088198', '2020-09-01 00:00:00', '1e0377ae', True, True)" .
chx:X_SignetGenesisShared rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SignetGenesisShared .
chx:X_SignetSizeToday a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SignetSizeToday ; rdfs:label "326,440 blocks, 2.27 times the book"@en ; skos:definition "The default signet stood on 2026-10-15 at height 326,440, 2.27 times the 143,619 blocks of the book's listing, near the 321,840 that ten-minute blocks since 2020-09-01 would give, and the book's own figure was about 150,000."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_SignetSizeToday a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = int(L.raw('mempool_signet_tip_height.txt')); d = (datetime.datetime(2026, 10, 15) - datetime.datetime(2020, 9, 1)).days; (n, round(n / 143619, 2), d * 144, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'blocks' + chr(34) + ': 143619'), 'about 150,000 blocks')) evaluates to (326440, 2.27, 321840, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = int(L.raw('mempool_signet_tip_height.txt')); d = (datetime.datetime(2026, 10, 15) - datetime.datetime(2020, 9, 1)).days; (n, round(n / 143619, 2), d * 144, L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', (chr(34) + 'blocks' + chr(34) + ': 143619'), 'about 150,000 blocks'))" ; chx:output "(326440, 2.27, 321840, True)" .
chx:X_SignetSizeToday rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SignetSizeToday .
chx:X_RegtestStartState a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RegtestStartState ; rdfs:label "the book's regtest listing"@en ; skos:definition "A fresh regtest node reports exactly the book's values: chain regtest, 0 blocks and 0 headers, difficulty 4.656542373906925e-10, median time 1296688602 and best block 0f9188f13cb7b2c71f2a335e3a4fc328bf5beb436012afca590b1a11466e2206."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_RegtestStartState a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); i = R['b1_info0']; (i['chain'], i['blocks'], i['headers'], i['bestblockhash'], i['difficulty'], i['mediantime'], i['chainwork'][-2:], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '0f9188f13cb7b2c71f2a335e3[...]b436012afca590b1a11466e2206', '4.656542373906925e-10', '1296688602')) evaluates to ('regtest', 0, 0, '0f9188f13cb7b2c71f2a335e3a4fc328bf5beb436012afca590b1a11466e2206', 4.656542373906925e-10, 1296688602, '02', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); i = R['b1_info0']; (i['chain'], i['blocks'], i['headers'], i['bestblockhash'], i['difficulty'], i['mediantime'], i['chainwork'][-2:], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '0f9188f13cb7b2c71f2a335e3[...]b436012afca590b1a11466e2206', '4.656542373906925e-10', '1296688602'))" ; chx:output "('regtest', 0, 0, '0f9188f13cb7b2c71f2a335e3a4fc328bf5beb436012afca590b1a11466e2206', 4.656542373906925e-10, 1296688602, '02', True)" .
chx:X_RegtestStartState rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RegtestStartState .
chx:X_RegtestHalvesEvery150 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RegtestHalvesEvery150 ; rdfs:label "25 at 150, 12.5 at 300"@en ; skos:definition "The reward on regtest halves every 150 blocks instead of every 210,000: 50 coins for heights 1 to 149, 25 from 150, 12.5 from 300 and 6.25 from 450."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_RegtestHalvesEvery150 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s = R['b2_subsidy']; ({h: L.subsidy(int(h), 150) for h in s} == s, sorted((int(h), v) for h, v in s.items()), L.chain_facts('regtest')['halving'], L.chain_facts('main')['halving']) evaluates to (True, [(1, 5000000000), (149, 5000000000), (150, 2500000000), (299, 2500000000), (300, 1250000000), (449, 1250000000), (450, 625000000), (500, 625000000)], 150, 210000)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s = R['b2_subsidy']; ({h: L.subsidy(int(h), 150) for h in s} == s, sorted((int(h), v) for h, v in s.items()), L.chain_facts('regtest')['halving'], L.chain_facts('main')['halving'])" ; chx:output "(True, [(1, 5000000000), (149, 5000000000), (150, 2500000000), (299, 2500000000), (300, 1250000000), (449, 1250000000), (450, 625000000), (500, 625000000)], 150, 210000)" .
chx:X_RegtestHalvesEvery150 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RegtestHalvesEvery150 .
chx:X_RegtestBalanceAfter500 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RegtestBalanceAfter500 ; rdfs:label "12462.5"@en ; skos:definition "After 500 blocks the wallet showed 12462.5 coins as spendable and 931.25 as immature, which the sums of the halving rewards of blocks 1 to 400 and 401 to 500 give, as in the book; mining the 500 blocks took 2.27 seconds in this run."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_RegtestBalanceAfter500 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b2_balances']['mine']; (R['b2_balance'], sum(L.subsidy(h, 150) for h in range(1, 401)) / 1e8, b['immature'], sum(L.subsidy(h, 150) for h in range(401, 501)) / 1e8, R['b2_mine500_seconds'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '12462.50000000')) evaluates to (12462.5, 12462.5, 931.25, 931.25, 2.27, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b2_balances']['mine']; (R['b2_balance'], sum(L.subsidy(h, 150) for h in range(1, 401)) / 1e8, b['immature'], sum(L.subsidy(h, 150) for h in range(401, 501)) / 1e8, R['b2_mine500_seconds'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', '12462.50000000'))" ; chx:output "(12462.5, 12462.5, 931.25, 931.25, 2.27, True)" .
chx:X_RegtestBalanceAfter500 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RegtestBalanceAfter500 .
chx:X_NoDefaultWallet a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:NoDefaultWallet ; rdfs:label "createwallet with an empty name"@en ; skos:definition "The book's commands do not run on Bitcoin Core 31.1: createwallet with the empty name '' is refused with 'Wallet name cannot be empty' (exit code 8), a fresh node has no wallet, and getnewaddress answers that no wallet is loaded."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_NoDefaultWallet a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b1_createwallet_empty_name']; (c['exit'], c['out'], R['b1_listwallets'], R['b1_nowallet']['error'][:50], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', ('createwallet ' + chr(34) + chr(34)))) evaluates to (8, 'error code: -8 error message: Wallet name cannot be empty', [], 'error code: -18 error message: No wallet is loaded', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b1_createwallet_empty_name']; (c['exit'], c['out'], R['b1_listwallets'], R['b1_nowallet']['error'][:50], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', ('createwallet ' + chr(34) + chr(34))))" ; chx:output "(8, 'error code: -8 error message: Wallet name cannot be empty', [], 'error code: -18 error message: No wallet is loaded', True)" .
chx:X_NoDefaultWallet rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_NoDefaultWallet .
chx:X_PipelineOrder a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:PipelineOrder ; rdfs:label "regtest, signet or testnet, mainnet"@en ; skos:definition "The three stages differ in what the code gives them: regtest has one dummy seed and no public peers, signet 2 seeds and a signed block rule, testnet3 5 seeds and the minimum-difficulty rule, mainnet 8 seeds, the order the book recommends."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:IO_PipelineOrder a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = {k: L.chain_facts(k) for k in ('regtest', 'signet', 'test', 'main')}; ([(k, v['seeds'], v['min_diff']) for k, v in f.items()], R['b9_chains']['signet']['extra'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'deploying each change first on regtest, then on signet or testnet, and finally into production')) evaluates to ([('regtest', 1, True), ('signet', 2, False), ('test', 5, True), ('main', 8, False)], [], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch11_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = {k: L.chain_facts(k) for k in ('regtest', 'signet', 'test', 'main')}; ([(k, v['seeds'], v['min_diff']) for k, v in f.items()], R['b9_chains']['signet']['extra'], L.has('book_ch11_blockchain.adoc', 'deploying each change first on regtest, then on signet or testnet, and finally into production'))" ; chx:output "([('regtest', 1, True), ('signet', 2, False), ('test', 5, True), ('main', 8, False)], [], True)" .
chx:X_PipelineOrder rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_PipelineOrder .
chx:X_BlockIsHeaderPlusTransactions chx:hasComponent chx:X_HeaderIs80Bytes .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_BlockIsHeaderPlusTransactions ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:hasComponent ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_HeaderIs80Bytes ; rdfs:comment "A block is a container: a small header, then a counter, then the transactions (Block is header plus transactions); the header is exactly 80 bytes (The header is 80 bytes)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_HeaderIs80Bytes chx:hasComponent chx:X_RootIsAlways32Bytes .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_HeaderIs80Bytes ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:hasComponent ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_RootIsAlways32Bytes ; rdfs:comment "The 80 bytes of the header are 4 for the version, 32 for the previous block hash, 32 for the merkle root (The header is 80 bytes); the root is the single 32-byte summary of the transactions in the header (Root is always32 bytes)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_MerkleblockForLightClients chx:hasComponent chx:X_HeaderIs80Bytes .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_MerkleblockForLightClients ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:hasComponent ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_HeaderIs80Bytes ; rdfs:comment "A merkleblock message holds the header and a merkle path, 248 bytes of which 80 are the header (Merkleblock for light clients); the fixed size of the header makes light clients possible (The header is 80 bytes)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_TargetCompactEncoding chx:hasConsequence chx:X_HashLeadingZeros .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_TargetCompactEncoding ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:hasConsequence ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_HashLeadingZeros ; rdfs:comment "The zeros of a block hash are the visible result of the rule that the hash, read as a number, must not exceed the target (Hash leading zeros); the header stores the target in 4 bytes (Target compact encoding)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_TargetCompactEncoding chx:hasConsequence chx:X_ChainWorkAccumulates .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_TargetCompactEncoding ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:hasConsequence ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_ChainWorkAccumulates ; rdfs:comment "Each header adds the work that its target stands for (Chain work accumulates); the work of one block at difficulty 1 is 0x100010001 (Target compact encoding)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 chx:hasConsequence chx:X_TamperingBreaksDescendants .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:hasConsequence ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_TamperingBreaksDescendants ; rdfs:comment "Because the previous-block field is part of the header and so of the hash, changing a block changes its own hash and breaks the link in the next block (Tampering breaks descendants; Block hash is double sha256)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_CoinbaseMaturity100 chx:hasConsequence chx:X_RegtestBalanceAfter500 .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_CoinbaseMaturity100 ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:hasConsequence ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_RegtestBalanceAfter500 ; rdfs:comment "The book's balance is correct only because rewards must be 100 blocks deep to be spent, and 931.25 coins stayed immature (Regtest balance after 500 blocks); the rule applies to every chain, regtest included (Coinbase maturity of 100 blocks)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_ChainWorkAccumulates chx:hasConsequence chx:X_ForkResolvedByMoreWork .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_ChainWorkAccumulates ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:hasConsequence ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_ForkResolvedByMoreWork ; rdfs:comment "A node follows the chain with the most accumulated work (Chain work accumulates); a fork is resolved when one branch becomes heavier (Fork resolved by more work)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_OddLeafDuplicated chx:hasConsequence chx:X_Cve20122459Trees .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_OddLeafDuplicated ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:hasConsequence ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_Cve20122459Trees ; rdfs:comment "The rule that an odd last hash is duplicated has a consequence: different lists of transactions can have the same merkle root (CVE-2012-2459 trees); the rule has a price which the section on the design flaw shows (Odd leaf duplicated)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_HeightIsNotUnique chx:refersTo chx:X_TwoChildrenOneParent .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_HeightIsNotUnique ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_TwoChildrenOneParent ; rdfs:comment "Two different children of the same parent were both at height 511 on the test chain (Height is not unique); that fork is the one the section on forks builds (Two children one parent)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_HeightFromGenesis chx:refersTo chx:X_GenesisHardcoded .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_HeightFromGenesis ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_GenesisHardcoded ; rdfs:comment "The genesis block sits at height 0 (Height from genesis); a fresh node reported height 0 and 0 headers because it knows only the genesis block built into its code (Genesis hardcoded)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_GlacierCoreAnalogy chx:refersTo chx:X_CoinbaseMaturity100 .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_GlacierCoreAnalogy ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_CoinbaseMaturity100 ; rdfs:comment "The 100 blocks of coinbase maturity are about 16.7 hours of the layers of the picture (Glacier core analogy; Coinbase maturity of 100 blocks)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_GenesisHashRecomputed chx:refersTo chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_GenesisHashRecomputed ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 ; rdfs:comment "The 80-byte genesis header is hashed twice to obtain the genesis hash (Genesis hash recomputed), which is the double SHA-256 of the header (Block hash is double sha256)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_ChancellorOfTheHeadline chx:refersTo chx:X_GenesisCoinbaseMessage .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_ChancellorOfTheHeadline ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_GenesisCoinbaseMessage ; rdfs:comment "The headline in the genesis block, on the Chancellor, is the text of the coinbase message (The Chancellor of the headline; Genesis coinbase message)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_ChancellorOfTheHeadline chx:refersTo chx:X_TimestampField .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_ChancellorOfTheHeadline ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_TimestampField ; rdfs:comment "The timestamp in the genesis header, 2009-01-03 18:15:05 UTC, falls on the same day as the issue (The Chancellor of the headline; Timestamp field)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_PreviousHashPointsToParent chx:refersTo chx:X_GenesisHardcoded .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_PreviousHashPointsToParent ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_GenesisHardcoded ; rdfs:comment "The sequence of hashes is the chain that runs back to the genesis block (Previous hash points to parent); a node follows the parent links back to the genesis block it already knows (Genesis hardcoded)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_NodeRejectsMutatedBlock chx:refersTo chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_NodeRejectsMutatedBlock ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 ; rdfs:comment "The mutated block has the same hash as the original, so a careless node could remember that hash as bad (Node rejects mutated block; Block hash is double sha256)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_SixtyFourByteWeakness chx:refersTo chx:X_MerkleblockForLightClients .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_SixtyFourByteWeakness ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_MerkleblockForLightClients ; rdfs:comment "A light client that checks a merkle path is the one at risk of mistaking a 64-byte transaction for an inner node (The 64-byte weakness; Merkleblock for light clients)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_TreeDepth chx:refersTo chx:X_PathLengthLogarithm .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_TreeDepth ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_PathLengthLogarithm ; rdfs:comment "Proving that one transaction is included takes about log2(N) hashes, the depth of the tree (Tree depth); the path grows with the logarithm of the count of transactions (Path length logarithm)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_BlockIsHeaderPlusTransactions chx:refersTo chx:X_GenesisListingMatchesBook .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_BlockIsHeaderPlusTransactions ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_GenesisListingMatchesBook ; rdfs:comment "The genesis block is 80 + 1 + 204 = 285 bytes (Block is header plus transactions); the book's listing of the genesis block agrees with the size 285 (Genesis listing matches book)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_SeveralChainsExist chx:refersTo chx:X_Testnet4Replaces .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_SeveralChainsExist ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_Testnet4Replaces ; rdfs:comment "The genesis hash 00000000da84f2ba... that the node of testnet4 reported (Several chains exist) is the hash of the genesis block of testnet4 (Testnet4 replaces testnet3)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_SeveralChainsExist chx:refersTo chx:X_SignetGenesisShared .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_SeveralChainsExist ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_SignetGenesisShared ; rdfs:comment "The genesis hash 00000008819873e9... that the node of the signet reported (Several chains exist) is the hash 000000088198... of the genesis block of every signet (Signet genesis shared)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_SeveralChainsExist chx:refersTo chx:X_RegtestStartState .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_SeveralChainsExist ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:refersTo ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_RegtestStartState ; rdfs:comment "The genesis hash 0f9188f1... that the node of regtest reported (Several chains exist) is the best block of a fresh regtest node (Regtest start state)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_HeightIsNotUnique chx:isComparedWith chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_HeightIsNotUnique ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:isComparedWith ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_BlockHashIsDoubleSha256 ; rdfs:comment "A block has two names: its hash identifies it uniquely, its height does not (Height is not unique; Block hash is double sha256)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_TestnetBlockStorms chx:isComparedWith chx:X_HeightFromGenesis .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_TestnetBlockStorms ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:isComparedWith ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_HeightFromGenesis ; rdfs:comment "Testnet3 had 5,189,394 blocks, more than 5 times the 971,537 blocks of mainnet (Testnet block storms; Height from genesis)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_PipelineOrder chx:isComparedWith chx:X_RegtestStartState .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_PipelineOrder ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:isComparedWith ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_RegtestStartState ; rdfs:comment "The stages differ in what the code gives them: regtest has one dummy seed and no peers (Pipeline order; Regtest start state)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_PipelineOrder chx:isComparedWith chx:X_SignetChallengeIsMultisig .
[] a owl:Axiom ; owl:annotatedSource chx:X_PipelineOrder ; owl:annotatedProperty chx:isComparedWith ; owl:annotatedTarget chx:X_SignetChallengeIsMultisig ; rdfs:comment "The stages differ in what the code gives them: signet has 2 DNS seeds and a block rule that needs a signature (Pipeline order; Signet challenge is a multisig)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch11/research> .
chx:X_PipelineOrder chx:isComparedWith chx:X_TestnetMinimumDifficulty .
